    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Offers in Excess of €395,000\r\nImmaculate 5-bedroom detached Residence of c 200 sqm with large paved driveway and expansive front lawn area incorporating an abundance of mature trees. The rear of the property features several lawn areas, glass house, metal garden shed, rose & herb garden, pergola, outdoor bar & grill, rear concrete yard overlooking beautiful country side with large detached garage / workshop of c 41 sqm and a side patio area and pergola. Build in c 2000, this property is in the centre of Ballycullane village with primary school, local sports grounds, super market & petrol station and pub. Located within only 10 minutes drive to historic Tintern Abbey with its extensive walking trails & beautiful Colclough walled garden and the sandy beaches of Duncannon & Fethard-on-Sea. The stunning coastline of the Hook Head Peninsula and New Ross Town with the Dunbrody Famine Ship are only c 15 minutes drive, Wexford Town and Waterford City ca 30 minutes away.\r\n\r\nIDEAL FAMILY / RETIREMENT HOME!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall   \t-\t4.76m x 2.18m carpet flooring, white PVC entrance door with glass insert & sidelights, ceiling coving and wooden staircase to top floor with carpet steps and under stairs storage space.\r\nInner Hallway     \t-  \t8.58m x 1.07m carpet flooring, ceiling coving and hot press / linen closet.\r\nLiving Room        \t-\t4.95m x 4.84m carpet flooring, ceiling coving, fireplace with electric stove insert, painted wood mantel and granite hearth, large Bay window overlooking front garden and gable window.\r\nKitchen / Dining\t- \t6.37m x 3.46m open plan with tile flooring, ceiling coving, solid wood and painted country kitchen, laminate counter tops, stainless sink, tile splash back, integrated electric cooker, dishwasher, fridge/freezer, and door access to utility and formal dining room / family lounge. \r\nUtility Room      \t-\t2.42m x 2.33m laminate flooring, stainless sink unit with laminate countertop and tile splash back, built-in cabinets, washer/dryer hook-up and white PVC back entry door with glass insert.\r\nDining Room    \t-\t4.21m x 3.47m currently used as family lounge with carpet flooring, ceiling coving, large windows and French doors to side patio area. \r\nBedroom 1      \t-\t4.08m x 3.61m carpet flooring and ceiling coving.\r\nBedroom 2      \t-\t3.62m x 3.43m carpet flooring and ceiling coving.\r\nBathroom        \t-\t3.45m x 2.02m tile flooring, fully tiled walls, large walk-in pressure shower, WC and WHB.\r\nTop Landing       \t-\t6.15m x 1.73m carpet flooring, vaulted ceiling with skylight, built-in linen closet and access to attic.\r\nBedroom 3      \t-\t2.85m x 2.30m tile flooring, fully tiled walls, large walk-in shower, WC and WHB.\r\nBedroom 4      \t-\t2.78m x 2.62m carpet flooring and vaulted ceiling with skylight.\r\nBedroom 5       \t-\t4.45m x 3.44m carpet flooring, vaulted ceiling and large gable window.\r\nGuest WC       \t-\t2.89m x 1.19m tile flooring, vaulted ceiling, skylight, WC, WHB."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Immaculate 5-Bedroom detached Residence of c 200 sqm.\r\nC 1 acre beautifully landscaped and private grounds with an abundance of shrubs and (fruit-) trees, herb & rose garden, side patio, pergola, outdoor bar & grill, mature front, side & rear lawn areas, large concrete rear yard, glass house and metal garden/storage shed.\r\nLarge detached garage / workshop 10.62m x 4.00m with insulated metal roof, plaster & painted exterior, roll-up door, electrics in, 7 windows and side entry door.\r\nPiers and metal gates, curbed and paved driveway with ample parking \r\nWhite PVC double-glazed windows, fascia & soffit, and slate roof.  \r\nDouble block cavity walls with easy maintenance pebble dash exterior finish.\r\nIn the centre of Ballycullane village with supermarket, petrol station, primary school, GAA sports park, church, pub etc.\r\nEasy commute to the towns of New Ross & Wexford and Waterford City. \r\nOnly minutes to beautiful coastline and beaches. \r\nClose proximity to famous Duncannon Beach and the Hook Head Peninsula."
      },
